[h2]One shared War Chest. Competing priorities.[/h2]
Commander In Chief is a top-down, vertically scrolling arcade shooter set in a fictional political-satire scenario. A caricatured commander fights through Iranian-themed enemy forces. The characters and encounters are stylized game fiction, not a reconstruction of actual military events.

Kills earn coins for the War Chest. Spend them on ammunition, grenades, protection and support, or keep a reserve for revives when the current mode permits them. In local co-op, both players draw from the same pool.

[h2]Read the attack. Choose your response.[/h2]
Move and aim independently while your machine gun fires automatically. Dodge marked firing lanes, use cover and throw grenades at armored threats. Board a tank to trade mobility and fuel for protection, crushing treads and a cannon that spends your grenade stock. In co-op, a partner can join as the gunner.

[h2]A campaign and repeatable challenges[/h2]
[list]
[*]Campaign: advance through six sectors to the Foundry Colossus and a final stand without revives.
[*]Endless War: survive escalating waves, restock between fights and earn Veteran Points for starting-loadout perks.
[*]Arcade and chapter select: start at a chosen campaign sector.
[*]Boss Rush: face a gunship gauntlet followed by the Colossus.
[*]Daily Run: take on a date-seeded challenge, with one bankable attempt per day on your local profile.
[*]Local records and replay: revisit your last recorded run and track results in the Hall of Fame.
[/list]

[h2]Solo or same-screen co-op[/h2]
Play alone or with a second local player. Share supplies, combine driver and gunner roles, and decide when to spend on a teammate's recovery. Player two uses a controller. This version does not include online co-op.

Options include remappable controls, Assist mode, reduced motion, color adjustments, text scaling and captions for supported voice and warning cues. These settings adjust presentation or difficulty; they do not remove the game's combat content.
